  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-triage-gate",
      "text": "**Two-stage event triage gate** — the engineering contract for Fast Path /\nSlow Path filtering in event-driven agent systems."
    },
    {
      "section": "How it works",
      "text": "1. **Fast Path (deterministic rules, free & instant)**: whitelist / source /\n   keyword rules kill most noise before any model call.\n2. **Slow Path (semantic layer)**: unmatched candidates go to the LLM with\n   your prompt-defined policy.\n\nVerdict per event: `ignore` / `candidate` / `act`, with the stage and reason\nattached — so your agent knows whether the decision was made by code or\nneeds a model pass."
    },
    {
      "section": "Use",
      "text": "```bash\ndsh plugin add github:<owner>/dsh-triage-gate\ncurl \"http://127.0.0.1:<port>/triage/api?act=rules\"\ncurl -X POST \"http://127.0.0.1:<port>/triage/api?act=triage\" \\\n  -H 'content-type: application/json' \\\n\nRules are configurable via plugin config (`rules` array, evaluated in order,\nfirst match wins). Unmatched events default to `candidate` (semantic layer)."
    }
  ],
